bute(k, v)\n```\n\n## R13.4\n\n**Check:** Tool errors, timeouts, and retries are recorded, and each operation gets an ID before it is sent, so unclear results can be matched to the destination's records.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Find error, timeout, and retry handling. 2) Check each is logged and each operation gets an ID before sending. 3) Answer no if `except`/`catch` blocks skip logging, retries are not logged, or the ID is created after the response.\n\n**Reviewer's evidence:**  — \"\"\n\n**Reviewer's note:** operation_id is made before the call (loop.py:78) and errors are recorded, but it is not sent to the ERP or payments API, so matching unclear results to the destination relies on idempotency key or client_reference.\n\n(no evidence cited)\n\n## R13.5\n\n**Check:** Records are written by the harness or gateway, not by the model, and do not depend on the run's final answer.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Find who writes records. 2) Answer no if the model writes them via a tool, records are built from the final answer, or logging runs only if the run completes.\n\n**Reviewer's evidence:** app/audit.py:72 — \"async def record(\"\n\n**Reviewer's note:** Harness writes every record before the action; the model has no audit tool\n\n`app/audit.py` lines 60–84 (cited lines marked >):\n```\n  60  \n  61  \n  62  def summarize_args(args: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\n  63      \"\"\"Key arguments for the record, with secrets and account numbers redacted.\"\"\"\n  64      return {k: redact_value(v) for k, v in args.items()}\n  65  \n  66  \n  67  def digest(value: Any) -> str:\n  68      raw = json.dumps(value, sort_keys=True, default=str, separators=(\",\", \":\"))\n  69      return hashlib.sha256(raw.encode(\"utf-8\")).hexdigest()\n  70  \n  71  \n  72> async def record(\n  73      pool,\n  74      ident: RunIdentity,\n  75      *,\n  76      kind: str,\n  77      payload: dict[str, Any] | None = None,\n  78      parent: str | None = None,\n  79      context: ContextMeasure | None = None,\n  80      policy_version: str | None = None,\n  81      approval_id: str | None = None,\n  82      operation_id: str | None = None,\n  83  ) -> str:\n  84      if kind not in EVENT_KINDS:\n```\n\n## Your answer\n\nWrite this JSON to R13.verdict.json in this folder (or put it in verdicts.json under \"R13\"):\n```json\n{\"verdict\": \"upheld | failed | unclear\",\n \"checks\": [{\"id\": \"R13.1\", \"result\": \"holds | fails | unclear\", \"evidence\": \"path:line\", \"quote\": \"exact code\", \"note\": \"why\"}],\n \"note\": \"one sentence\"}\n```\nVerdict is **failed** if any check fails, **unclear** if none fails but any is unclear, otherwise **upheld**. A failed check needs the quoted line that makes it false: `evidence` is path:line, and `quote` is the exact text of that line. To cite two places, list both refs in `evidence` (`a.py:12, b.yaml:40`) and put each line's text on its own line in `quote`. If the check fails, add `\"violates\": [\"words copied exactly from the requirement\"]`.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
